What good looks like

* One enterprise capability model for unstructured data to AI, aligned to the reference architecture and reusable across platforms.
* Federated adoption by data platform, with common standards, contracts, and controls rather than isolated local implementations.
* Shared building blocks for ingestion, preparation, semantic processing, governed persistence, retrieval, and publication.
* A governed operating model covering classification, lineage, audit, residency, IAM, and embedding model governance end to end.
* New use cases onboard through a repeatable, evidence-led path, reducing bespoke design and accelerating delivery.

Scope guardrails

* We are not creating one central monolithic unstructured data platform for the whole bank.
* We are not building use-case-specific prompt logic, ranking logic, or business workflow orchestration inside shared services.
* We are not bypassing enterprise controls such as security, privacy, model risk, TPRM, audit, or change governance.
* We are not trying to build every adjacent capability at once; delivery will focus on the highest-value reusable building blocks first.
* VectorDBaaS is one shared service within the wider workstream, not the entirety of the unstructured architecture.